          <li>MDN Web Docs, <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Exif" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">EXIF</a> (embedded metadata, including capture date and GPS, per the CIPA Exif standard), and <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Lossy_compression" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lossy</a> and <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Lossless_compression" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lossless compression</a>, 2025.</li>
          <li>Google for Developers, <a href="https://developers.google.com/speed/webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WebP</a> and the <a href="https://developers.google.com/speed/webp/docs/webp_study" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WebP Compression Study</a> (lossy WebP 25 to 34% smaller than JPEG; lossless 26% smaller than PNG; supported in all major browsers), 2025.</li>
          <li>Google Search Central, <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/page-experience" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Understanding Google page experience</a> (Core Web Vitals are used by ranking systems), current.</li>
